// UNSOUNDNESS repro (reviewer finding A3): `a == *` treated as a binding
// equality. A wildcard resolves to no value at evaluation, so the "binding"
// never happens and the whole guard is permanently false — a validated,
// dead forbid guard (fail-open), the same failure class as an unclosed
// leaf. A wildcard must not count as a resolvable value side: `a == *` is
// not a restrictor, leaving `a` unrestricted here — rejected.
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (a: Long). (a == * && a > 100)
};
